Attributions
------------

The model weights were trained on synthetic pairs derived from the following
recordings:

  Kimiko Ishizaka, "J.S. Bach: The Well-Tempered Clavier, Book 1"
  (Open Well-Tempered Clavier, https://welltemperedclavier.org/).
  The project site describes the recording as released into the public
  domain; the Bandcamp release used here was labelled CC BY 4.0, so it is
  attributed under that license:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Changes: segmented, and degraded with a recording-chain simulator.

  Kimiko Ishizaka, "Open Goldberg Variations" (CC0 1.0).
  Musopen, "Complete Chopin Collection" (CC0 1.0).

The degradation simulator was calibrated with measurements from:

  O. Mikkonen, A. Wright, E. Moliner, V. Valimaki, "Neural Modeling of
  Magnetic Tape Recorders", DAFx 2023. Dataset licensed under CC BY 4.0,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.8026271.
  Changes: hiss segments, frequency response and wow/flutter were measured
  from the dataset; the dataset itself is not redistributed.

Recordings from the UCSB Discography of American Historical Recordings
(https://adp.library.ucsb.edu) were used for evaluation only, under DAHR's
terms of use. No DAHR audio is part of
the training data of the released weights, and none is redistributed.
